    {
      "id": "simon",
      "name": "Simon Whitlock",
      "role": "Clara's husband; investor, of Whitlock Holdings",
      "age": 38,
      "portrait": "man-bare",
      "color": "#5f7a4e",
      "personality": "Boyish, quick and charming, the man everybody likes for the first hour. He has talked his way out of every bill and every scrape of his life and assumes he can talk his way out of this one. Underneath the charm is months of panic. He plays the grieving son-in-law and overplays it, and when he is cornered he offers a new story rather than admit the old one was false.",
      "speech_style": "Easy, warm, clubby talk: 'old man', 'dear fellow', 'honestly, Detective', 'the thing is'. Laughs at his own jokes. Calls Edmund 'the old boy' and then corrects himself to 'Edmund'. When nervous he talks too fast and piles on details nobody asked for: names, times, the color of somebody's tie.",
      "alibi": "Just after nine I went out to the hall telephone and rang my broker, Ambrose Kittredge, at his house in the city. Dull business about Monday's market. We talked until about twenty past and then I went straight back to the drawing room. The line must have gone down after I hung up.",
