          "condition": "free"
        },
        {
          "clue_id": "danny-vance-booth",
          "text": "Says Mr. Vance sat in Booth 9 by the back corridor all night, and was still there ordering a last brandy and a soda just before midnight.",
          "condition": "pressed"
        },
        {
          "clue_id": "danny-debt",
          "text": "Admits he owed Mr. Kale $400 from the Thursday card game and that the $400 in his pocket was meant to pay it at midnight. He went to the office at 00:05 to pay and found Kale dead.",
          "condition": "shown_evidence:danny-iou"
        },
        {
          "clue_id": "danny-alley",
          "text": "Admits he was not behind the bar during the solo: he slipped out the kitchen door and met Lena in the laundry doorway, where she gave him the $400 in the bank envelope. They were together from about 23:36 to 23:44. While they stood there, a man in a dark overcoat and a low hat hurried past from the dead end by the office door toward River Street, but Danny kept his face turned away and never saw the man's.",
          "condition": "shown_evidence:cash-envelope"
        }
      ],
      "breaks_on": ["cash-envelope", "danny-iou"],
      "patience": 11,
      "deflections": [
        "*wipes the same glass for the third time*  Look, look, look, I told the other cops already, sir.",
        "*jams his shaking hands into his apron*  Can I get some air? Just a minute.",
        "*stares at the office door*  I keep seeing him in there. I can't. Not right now.",
        "*swallows hard*  You want me to say I did something I didn't do? I won't, Officer. Sir."
      ],
      "alibi_verification": {
        "status": "broken",
        "evidence_ids": ["cash-envelope"],
        "clue_ids": ["lena-alley"],
        "note": "He was not behind the bar: he was in the laundry doorway with Lena from about 23:36 to 23:44, as her envelope and her confession show. He does not know the safe combination, and he was carrying the $400 to pay Kale, not to kill him."
      }
    }
  ],
  "hints": [
    "Nobody in a packed club heard a shot. Find out when the room was at its loudest: the bandstand can tell you, and so can the coroner's window.",
    "Every one of these four has lied about where they were during the drum solo. Pin each story to the board, then search each room for the thing that contradicts it: a bar chit, a pair of shoes, an envelope in the rain.",
    "The gun went into the water, but it came out of a safe. Search the alley, then read the cards on the bar safe and ask the bartender who can open it.",
    "Kale's desk was torn apart but his cash box was left full. Whoever searched it was after a document, and Kale was the kind of man who hid things behind other things.",
    "Leonard Vance swears he went home before 23:30. The bar's time clock says otherwise. Show him his own chit and ask what he saw from Booth 9.",
    "Lena and Danny Marsh are covering for each other. Show either of them the bank envelope from the laundry doorway, then ask yourself who walked past them in the rain, and who came back in through the front soaking wet.",
    "Look hard at Frank Dellow: combine the black notebook behind the painting, the revolver from the rain barrel, and Leonard Vance's signed statement."
  ],
  "endings": {
    "correct": "Frank Dellow takes the cuffs like a man settling a tab he always knew would come due. The black notebook, the gun from the rain barrel and the lawyer's statement close the books on the Blue Lantern for good. Outside, the rain keeps falling on Riverside.",
    "wrong_culprit": "The cuffs close on the wrong wrists, and the real killer holds the door for you on your way out. By Monday the Blue Lantern has a new owner, a new set of books and a manager who smiles at you every time you pass.",
    "weak_proof": "You have the right man, and he knows it, but any lawyer in Calder City could drive a truck through your case. Without the motive, the gun and a witness who saw him leave the door, the District Attorney will not touch it. Frank Dellow walks out into the rain whistling, and you go back inside to find what you missed."
  }
