    "description": "Chief clerk of Ashgrove Shipping for thirty-one years, a widower who lived for his ledgers and was known on the waterfront for keeping a carbon copy of nearly everything he wrote.",
    "cause_of_death": "A single heavy blow to the left temple and a broken neck at the foot of the archive stairs, first reported as a fall. The police surgeon puts death between 22:45 and 23:30.",
    "found_in": "archive",
    "found_at": "at 06:00 by the night watchman, at the foot of the iron stairs"
