        {
          "clue_id": "vance-meeting",
          "text": "Admits he met Pike in the archive at ten last night, that Pike caught his sleeve at the steel cabinet, and that he left at half past ten for the 22:40 Eastbank ferry. Pike was alive and back at his desk with a folder of cargo manifests and the telephone directory open at the Customs House page.",
          "condition": "shown_evidence:vance-cufflink"
        },
        {
          "clue_id": "vance-ferry",
          "text": "Admits the Vance and Pryor account ticket in the slip-man's book is his: he sailed to Eastbank at 22:40 and could not have come back before the 23:50 crossing. Pike was alive when he left the pier.",
          "condition": "shown_evidence:ferry-log"
        },
        {
          "clue_id": "vance-deadline",
          "text": "Admits Pike had given him until the first of May to repay the trust or face the Bar Association. He went to settle it privately; Pike would not sell the folder and said the Harbor Commission would hear 'the customs business' first, at nine, and Vance could wait his turn.",
          "condition": "shown_evidence:trust-dossier"
