  "hints": [
    "Harold Pike had somewhere to be at nine this morning. Find out where, and about what: his typewriter in the front office and his tally desk in the warehouse both have something to say.",
    "Most of these people are lying about something smaller than murder. Pin every story to the clock: the police surgeon's window runs from 22:45 to 23:30.",
    "Leonard Vance has the loudest motive and a cufflink in the archive. Show him the cufflink, then read the ferry slip tally book on the dock and the ferry clock beside it. Where was he when the window opened?",
    "Tommy's watchman's clock says he never walked a round after nine. Show him the dial. A man who sat at the gatehouse window all night saw more than he admits.",
    "Clara Ashgrove buried a warning about the manifests, but the gatehouse telephone pad says where she was at eleven. She had a motive and no time to act on it.",
